      "notes": "[Read concept note](./notes/Sequence.md)"
    },
    "Set": {
      "title": "Set",
      "type": "Mathematical Logic and Foundations",
      "define": "A set is a collection of distinct objects considered as a single mathematical object.",
      "notes": "[Read concept note](./notes/Set.md)"
    },
    "Tensor": {
      "title": "Tensor",
      "type": "Algebra",
      "define": "A tensor is a multilinear object that generalizes scalars, vectors, covectors, and linear maps.",
      "notes": "[Read concept note](./notes/Tensor.md)"
    }
